The Qur'an gives the reason we must know ourselves. Surah al-Shams opens with a run of oaths: by the sun and the moon, the day and the night,[-and-] the sky and {+Him who built it, and+} the earth {+and Him who spread it+} (Q 91:1–6). The last oath is by the soul and "Him who fashioned it, and inspired it with [discernment between] its virtues and vices" (Q 91:7–8). Every soul comes with the means to tell good from evil, and the next two verses say what follows from that gift.

::: {.ayah ref="91:9-10"}
one who purifies it is felicitous, and one who betrays it fails.
